Subject: [PATCH] susfs: add missing struct inode decl in compat_fillonedir

The combined susfs4ksu kernel-4.14 patch inserts `inode = ilookup(...)`
code into compat_fillonedir (fs/readdir.c) but does NOT insert the
matching `struct inode *inode;` declaration. This causes Clang 12 to
fail with:

  fs/readdir.c:592:2: error: must use 'struct' tag to refer to type 'inode'
  fs/readdir.c:593:7: error: use of undeclared identifier 'inode'

All four other filldir variants (fillonedir, filldir, filldir64,
compat_filldir) have BOTH a decl hunk AND a use hunk. compat_fillonedir
has only the use hunk.

Fix: insert the missing decl after compat_ulong_t d_ino.
---
--- a/fs/readdir.c
+++ b/fs/readdir.c
@@ -390,6 +390,9 @@ static int compat_fillonedir(struct dir_context *ctx, const char *name,
 	struct compat_readdir_callback *buf =
 		container_of(ctx, struct compat_readdir_callback, ctx);
 	struct compat_old_linux_dirent __user *dirent;
 	compat_ulong_t d_ino;
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_PATH
+	struct inode *inode;
+#endif
 
 	if (buf->result)
 		return -EINVAL;
